Corrections to defects in testall.asm itself, applied before assembly.
The vendored file stays byte-identical to upstream; see PROVENANCE.

Instruction test 29, second case: the check `subb a,#24h` (with the carry
DA leaves set) passes only when DA yields A=0x25, the BCD sum 58+67=125.
The operand as written is 56h, whose BCD sum with 67h is 123 - the test
can never pass on a correct implementation of DA A.

--- a/testall.asm
+++ b/testall.asm
@@ -987,7 +987,7 @@
 tst2:
 	mov psw, #00h
 	mov r3, #67h
-	mov a, #56h
+	mov a, #58h
 	addc a, r3
 	da  a
 	subb a, #24h
